From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: v8-embed-feedstock <noreply@github.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Link the whole engine into the Windows DLL

A component build of V8 links one shared library out of static
libraries, and a linker pulls out of a static library only what
something already in the link refers to.  v8dll-main.cc refers to
nothing, so the engine's exported API -- in objects nothing references
-- stays out.  gyp's ninja generator handles that on Linux by itself:
its solink rule wraps the inputs in --whole-archive.  v8.gyp handles it
on macOS with -all_load.  On Windows nobody does, and the result is an
8 KB v8.dll, an import library with nothing in it, and a consumer that
fails to link every V8 symbol it uses.

link.exe and lld-link have the equivalent, /WHOLEARCHIVE:<library>, and
it goes on the six libraries that make up V8 itself: the base, the
compiler, the initializers, libbase, libplatform and the snapshot.
That is where every V8_EXPORT lives.  ICU, abseil, highway, zlib and
simdutf are left to be pulled in by reference, which is all the DLL
needs of them.

The option takes a file, not a name: lld-link opens exactly what it is
given ("could not open 'v8_base_without_compiler.lib'" when given the
bare name), so the path has to be spelled the way each generator lays
the libraries out -- $(OutDir)lib\ under MSBuild, obj\<gyp dir>\ under
ninja, relative to the build directory the link runs in.
---

diff --git a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
--- a/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
+++ b/tools/v8_gypfiles/v8.gyp
@@ -2178,6 +2178,39 @@
                 'OTHER_LDFLAGS': ['-dynamiclib', '-all_load']
               },
             }],
+            # link.exe takes from a static library only what is referenced,
+            # and nothing references the exported API.  The unix linkers get
+            # --whole-archive / -all_load for this; this is the same thing.
+            # /WHOLEARCHIVE wants a file it can open, and the two generators
+            # put static libraries in different places.
+            ['OS=="win" and GENERATOR=="msvs"', {
+              'msvs_settings': {
+                'VCLinkerTool': {
+                  'AdditionalOptions': [
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:$(OutDir)lib\\v8_base_without_compiler.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:$(OutDir)lib\\v8_compiler.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:$(OutDir)lib\\v8_initializers.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:$(OutDir)lib\\v8_libbase.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:$(OutDir)lib\\v8_libplatform.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:$(OutDir)lib\\v8_snapshot.lib',
+                  ],
+                },
+              },
+            }],
+            ['OS=="win" and GENERATOR=="ninja"', {
+              'msvs_settings': {
+                'VCLinkerTool': {
+                  'AdditionalOptions': [
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:obj\\tools\\v8_gypfiles\\v8_base_without_compiler.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:obj\\tools\\v8_gypfiles\\v8_compiler.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:obj\\tools\\v8_gypfiles\\v8_initializers.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:obj\\tools\\v8_gypfiles\\v8_libbase.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:obj\\tools\\v8_gypfiles\\v8_libplatform.lib',
+                    '/WHOLEARCHIVE:obj\\tools\\v8_gypfiles\\v8_snapshot.lib',
+                  ],
+                },
+              },
+            }],
             ['soname_version!=""', {
               'product_extension': 'so.<(soname_version)',
             }],
